You use Internal Revenue Service (IRS) Form 4547, titled Trump Account Election(s), to elect to establish the account and request the one-time $1,000 pilot program contribution. An authorized individual, such as a legal guardian, parent, adult sibling, or grandparent, files the form to establish the account for an eligible child under age 18. You can submit Form 4547 at any time, including by e-filing it alongside your current-year income tax return or through trumpaccounts.gov when online elections open in mid-2026. For a child born after December 31, 2024 and before January 1, 2029, check line 7 in Part III to request the initial government contribution, or leave line 7 blank if the child only qualifies for the standard account election described in our guide on [how to open a Trump Account](/guides/how-to-open-a-trump-account/).